1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,069
People don't quit the game.

2
00:00:02,069 --> 00:00:03,738
They quit organizing it.

3
00:00:03,738 --> 00:00:06,194
Six messages, and still no game.

4
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,810
This is Serve, built during this hackathon.

5
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:13,197
Your agent works out your week with your friends' agents; you say yes once.

6
00:00:13,197 --> 00:00:17,222
It runs on Muse Glimmer, on my own RTX 3090.

7
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,244
Act one: cold start.

8
00:00:19,244 --> 00:00:22,252
I ask my agent for one more player on Saturday.

9
00:00:22,252 --> 00:00:28,253
Muse Glimmer drafts the invite with the nearest court, and Llama Guard checks it before anyone sees it.

10
00:00:28,253 --> 00:00:31,174
I post it, and share the link to any group chat.

11
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,978
Leo has no account.

12
00:00:35,978 --> 00:00:39,324
The link opens the game, one sign-in, and he's in.

13
00:00:39,324 --> 00:00:42,127
The game is full, and I hear: game on.

14
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:50,804
Act two: agents negotiate.

15
00:00:50,804 --> 00:00:52,587
One tap plans my week.

16
00:00:52,587 --> 00:01:00,505
My agent talks to each member's agent over A2A, with signed Agent Cards; in this demo club, the members are simulated.

17
00:01:00,505 --> 00:01:03,526
The plan took 78 seconds, in the background.

18
00:01:03,526 --> 00:01:06,985
Everyone agreed, and nothing is booked until I say yes.

19
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:12,885
Or in Messenger: one yes, and it's booked.

20
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:19,648
And it's a real negotiation: Hana's agent counter-offers Saturday.

21
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,289
Act three: courts and clubs.

22
00:01:23,289 --> 00:01:25,372
Real courts from OpenStreetMap.

23
00:01:25,372 --> 00:01:33,544
Prompt Guard screens the reviews first, then Glimmer judges every court, and each reason cites the map, a review or the forecast.

24
00:01:33,544 --> 00:01:37,041
Clubs sit on a real map too, and anyone can start one.

25
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:50,635
Beyond text: send a video, like this sample clip, and it's auto-cut into a clip to share with your club.

26
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:54,355
Six Meta models carry Serve, with Muse Glimmer at the center.

27
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:56,529
Glimmer needs forty seconds.

28
00:01:56,529 --> 00:02:04,211
The 1B model I fine-tuned on its choices needs under one, and agrees with it 89.5 percent of the time.

29
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,620
Ninety-three scripted attacks, all stopped, and 37 of 42 unsafe messages refused.

30
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:14,884
It's live: eight people so far, me included, and three games filled.

31
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:20,665
And it works for school clubs, older adults, a charity cup: any ball sport.

32
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:22,908
Serve.

33
00:02:22,908 --> 00:02:23,893
Play more.

34
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:25,168
Manage less.

